A large potion shop in the early game is a significant
boon mainly because it eliminates the need to carry one
of each kind of potion to a shop where you can price
check them (typically, Minetown, or sometimes an early
general store).  This is particularly significant for
roles with low starting strength, especially when you
don't find an early bag of holding.  A large potion
shop lets you quickly put prices to most of the potion
types, which greatly facilitates early identification.

However, it'll be mid-game before it's worth buying out
the inventory (since early-game gold is better spent on
protection, magic armor if you find that in a shop, and
certain tools if you find a hardware), and by mid-game
you will have already accumulated more potions than
even a quite enormous potion shop can sell you.  (What
is the theoretical maximum shop size, anyway?  About
forty items?)

